<title>USA: Gerber Scientific Q3 shr $0.18 vs $0.22.</title>
<headline>Gerber Scientific Q3 shr $0.18 vs $0.22.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH WINDSOR, Conn. 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Quarter Financial Figures for</p>
<p>Three Months Ended Jan. 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p> Sales				     $94,591,000    $86,884,000</p>
<p> Net earnings				4,144,000	5,151,000</p>
<p> Net earnings per share(1)		     .18		.22</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	   23,357,000     23,516,000</p>
<p>			     Financial Figures for Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>Jan. 31, 1997 and 1996</p>
<p>						   1997		 1996</p>
<p> Sales				  $275,350,000     $265,233,000</p>
<p> Net earnings(1)			10,882,000	 15,177,000</p>
<p> Net earnings per share(1)		   .47		  .64</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding	 23,352,000	 23,808,000</p>
<p>(1) Included in this year's nine months ended Jan. 31, 1997 was a tax-exempt gain of $1,032,000 ($.04 per share) resulting from life insurance benefits the company received upon the death of H. Joseph Gerber.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
